{"uncertainty": 0.25, "outcome": "Submitted a property module and a single-task SymbiYosys prove setup for the approved deep_counter RTL at its default LIMIT of 99. They are ready for the platform to run formal.run and formal.cover. No tool has run, and nothing here is verified.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "assertions", "title": "deep_counter interface properties and covers", "summary": "Immediate-form assertions, one per rule of the approved interface spec [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.interface-spec.a1]: DC-RESET, DC-CLEAR (including en and clr high together), DC-COUNT step and wrap, DC-HOLD, DC-RANGE and DC-CARRY. They check the approved RTL [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.design-under-test.a1] through its ports in mode prove (unbounded k-induction with smtbmc), serving [requirement:req-8ed9eb1797]. The setup has no assume statements. DC-RANGE also serves as the helper invariant that makes induction close. Covers reach count == LIMIT, the top bit of count, carry, the wrap, clear during a count and reset during a count. Depth 110 is set because the first wrap is at step 101."}], "files": [{"path": "deep_counter.sby", "kind": "formal_spec", "title": "SymbiYosys prove setup for deep_counter", "summary": "Single-task setup with no [tasks] section, mode prove, depth 110, engine smtbmc. It reads the approved deep_counter.v [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.design-under-test.a1] by name and the property file, both listed under [files], with top deep_counter_props. The setup gives an unbounded proof, as [requirement:req-8ed9eb1797] asks. Depth 110 lets the same setup in cover mode reach the first wrap at LIMIT 99, at step 101, as the verification notes of [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.interface-spec.a1] require.", "entry": "deep_counter_props"}, {"path": "deep_counter_props.sv", "kind": "assertions", "title": "deep_counter property wrapper", "summary": "Top module that instantiates deep_counter [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.design-under-test.a1] with free inputs and asserts each behaviour rule of [artifact:prj-784d6227b5.interface-spec.a1]. A guard makes every $past use safe in the first cycle. DC-RANGE is gated on a reset-seen flag rather than on an assumption, and covers are included for vacuity checking. Serves [requirement:req-8ed9eb1797].", "entry": "deep_counter_props"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Expected to be 1-inductive: once reset has been seen, count <= LIMIT is preserved by every transition of the approved RTL. This is reasoning only; no formal.run has been executed.", "Expected cover reachability at depth 110: count == LIMIT first at step 100, the first wrap at step 101, carry at step 100, count[6] from step 65. This is reasoning only; no formal.cover has been executed.", "The rules are proved for the default LIMIT = 99 only; other LIMIT values in 1 to 127 (DC-PARAM) are not covered by this single-task setup.", "Before the first reset, count is undefined by the spec, so DC-RANGE and the DC-COUNT step are not asserted for count values above LIMIT before reset. DC-RESET, DC-CLEAR, DC-HOLD, DC-CARRY and the DC-COUNT wrap are asserted from cycle 1 regardless of reset."], "escalation": null, "notes": "No assume statements, so the inputs are constrained minimally. DC-RANGE is placed under a reset-seen flag rather than an assumed reset, because the RTL has no initial value for count. The DC-COUNT step assertion is guarded by $past(count) < LIMIT, so it never claims behaviour that is unspecified before reset; after reset, DC-RANGE makes that guard equivalent to count != LIMIT. All assertions are immediate statements in always blocks, the subset the open Yosys front end reads. Their guards are plain if chains, so the antecedent derivation of formal.cover can place a cover on each path. The prove mode and the depth are read from the setup by the gate. formal.cover reuses smtbmc and depth 110, which is why abc pdr was not chosen. A mutant that loses the wrap or the carry only after 100 enabled cycles is caught by the DC-COUNT wrap and DC-CARRY assertions in the unbounded proof, not by a bounded unroll. Independent review is still required before approval."}

